-- title:
--   Finite-type stable subalgebra localising to an end of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $C$ denotes `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, `jChartFin` denotes $j$ regarded as an element of $C$, `XFin` is $\operatorname{Spec} C$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained as the pushout glueing `XFin` to the spectrum of the analogous algebra attached to $j^{-1}$ along the common middle chart, with `ιFin` the canonical morphism from `XFin` into it and `toBase` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. For $p$ a natural number and $\Omega$ a field, [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) is the set of $x \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no non-zero point killed by $p$. Finally [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q O`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) is $X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1$ in $O[[X_0,X_1]]$.
--
--   **Data.** Primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \mid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$ together with the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$; a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$) with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ which by `hK` is the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$; a henselian discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$; an element $j \in K$, non-zero, whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathsf{j}$ of the modular $j$-function (`hj`); a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (`hϖ`); an element $\varpi_t \in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`); and a maximal ideal $y \subseteq C$ containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin}) \in$ `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart package `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of the two-chart model at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` and satisfying the supersingularity condition above for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and an isomorphism $e$ of the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f u\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses: $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; $C$ is stable under every automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; such $\tau$ fixes $y'$ pointwise modulo $y'$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$; for each such $\tau$ fixing $y'$ modulo $y'$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ compatible with $\tau$ through the germ map, the completion map and $e$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ trivial on constants, linear part given by $M$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M \equiv c\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, and having tangent directions $(a_1 : b_1)$, $(a_2 : b_2)$ with $a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ not divisible by $q$, contract to distinct ideals of the stalk; for a prime $P$ of $S$ with tangent direction $(1 : 0)$, the germ of $a \in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ exactly when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and `jqNModC L q` (the $j$-expansion with exponents multiplied by $q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0 \in A$, and its image in $S$ is the class of a series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ leading form is a unit at every pair $(a,b)$ in $W$, not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its explicit chart.** A point $z$ of the model, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of `XFin` over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`); a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$, for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the seven clauses just listed, verbatim for this data.
--
--   **The blow-up chart.** $J \subseteq C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the preimage, along the germ map $C \to \mathcal{O}_z$ followed by completion followed by $e_1$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, and then its preimage under the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. By `hB`, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`) is given, and: `hR1` (two clauses) says $C \subseteq B$ and that every $f \in K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2` (three clauses) says $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most one; `hR3` (five clauses) says $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$, $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, $b \in C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the elements outside $\mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` consists of five clauses: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation) with kernel $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k \to$ `CoordRing`, and equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$, such that $\rho \circ \tau$ equals the corresponding action `hAction` composed with $\rho$, and $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, in that $\tau$ maps every $b \in B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ into $B$ and into $Q$; an element $b \in B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserves $W$ as soon as it preserves $y$ on $C$.
--
--   **The end.** A subring $O$ of $K$ is given for which `hO` provides a non-zero $a \in J$ such that, writing $B_a$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x$ with $xa \in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (that is, $f \in O$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$), every element of $y$ being a non-unit of $O$, and $B \not\subseteq O$. Further, $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`). The last hypothesis `hIgStab` asserts that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is the image of $A$, such that $\varpi$ lies in $V$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, such that $C \subseteq V$, and such that some $c \in C$ has $p(c)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[X]$, is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $K$ such that:
--
--   1. every element of $B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$;
--
--   2. $B_x$ is of finite type over $A$;
--
--   3. for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau : K \simeq_L K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ (in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) with root of unity $\zeta$, scaling $q$ and level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$), $\tau$ maps $B_x$ into itself;
--
--   4. $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its elements which are units of $O$: for $f \in K$, $f \in O$ if and only if there are $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever it lies in $O$, and $fh = g$;
--
--   5. for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is the image of $A$ and in which $\varpi$, if it lies in $V$ at all, lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$: if $j \in V$ and every value $p(j)$, $p \in A[X]$ monic, that lies in $V$ is a unit of $V$, and if some element of $O$ is not in $V$, then some element of $B_x$ is not in $V$.
--
--   Here `IsLevelAutAt` unfolds to the requirement that $\tau$ implement the action of the matrix $\gamma^{-1}$, conjugated as $\begin{pmatrix}\gamma_{00} & \gamma_{01}/q\\ q\gamma_{10} & \gamma_{11}\end{pmatrix}$, on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, read through any embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$.
--
--   This is the step which replaces an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart by an affine neighbourhood of finite type over $A$: the local ring $O$ at a point of the blow-up outside the $\varpi_t$-chart is exhibited as a localisation of a finitely generated, level-automorphism-stable $A$-subalgebra of $B \cap O$, with a valuative separation property that lets the valuation rings missed by $O$ be detected inside that subalgebra. It is stated in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ frame, with a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ and the diamond condition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ in place of a full auxiliary level, so that it also applies for small $q$, and it feeds the assembly of the end chart with its pole data in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
